8
00:01:46,612 --> 00:02:12,907
好，我们言归正传，复习一下 Peter 讲过的内容，因为这套关于向量空间、基、线性算子和矩阵的内容极为基础，它为我们提供了许多极好的范例。记住第 4 章不是讲向量空间，而是讲线性算子。
Okay, let's go back and go over some of the material that Peter covered, because this business with vector spaces, bases, linear operators, and matrices is just fundamental, allows us to—gives us a lot of good examples. And so remember Chapter 4 is not about vector spaces, but about linear operators.

9
00:02:12,907 --> 00:02:40,988
所以在本讲中，V 和 W 将是域 F 上的有限维向量空间，我们再次希望看到任意域上的向量空间能得出什么结论，而不必局限于实数域或复数域。在本讲中，设 T 是从 V 到 W 的线性算子。
So V and W in this lecture will be finite-dimensional vector spaces over the field F, and again we want to see what we can do about vector spaces over any field, not necessarily the real numbers or the complex numbers. And in this lecture let T be a linear operator from V to W.

10
00:02:40,988 --> 00:02:55,082
用向量空间的语言来说它就是一个同态：保持加法，且保持标量乘法。
So that's just a homomorphism in the language of vector spaces: it preserves the addition and it preserves the scalar multiplication.

11
00:02:55,082 --> 00:03:06,738
一个著名的线性算子，而且某种意义上是线性算子理论之基石的，就是求导。
So a famous linear operator, and in one sense the the basis of the theory of linear operators, is differentiation.

12
00:03:06,738 --> 00:03:32,518
如果我们的第一个向量空间例如是域 F 上次数不超过 n 的 x 的多项式空间，第二个向量空间是次数不超过 n - 1 的 x 的多项式空间——这是维数为 n + 1 的有限维向量空间，而这是维数为 n 的有限维向量空间，
So if our first vector space were, for example, the polynomials in x over F of degree less than or equal to n, and our second vector space were the polynomials in x of degree less than or equal to n - 1—so this is a finite-dimensional vector space of dimension n + 1, this is a finite-dimensional vector space of dimension n,

13
00:03:32,518 --> 00:03:55,150
记住还包含常数项——那么存在一个线性算子 d/dx，是映射从 V 到 W，即如果你取一个次数不超过 n 的多项式并对 x 求导，就会得到一个次数不超过n - 1 的多项式，对吧？
remember you have the constants—then there's a linear operator d/dx is a map from V to W, namely if you take a polynomial whose degree is less than or equal to n and you differentiate it with respect to x, you get a polynomial of degree less than or equal to n - 1, correct?

14
00:03:55,150 --> 00:04:08,520
而且它是线性的，因为求导公式满足两函数之和的导数等于它们导数之和，常数乘以函数的导数等于常数乘以该函数的导数。
And it's linear because you have the formulas for differentiation: that you differentiate the sum of two functions you get the sum of their derivatives, and if you differentiate a constant times a function you get a constant times the derivative of the function.

15
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:25,279
在实数域上固然如此，但你也可以按通常的代数法则对任意域上的多项式求导，因此它在任何域上都适用。正是微积分的研究将线性算子引入了数学，而不是相反。
Well, that's over the real numbers, but you can differentiate polynomials over any field by the usual algebraic rules, so it works over any field. And the study of calculus is what brought linear operators into mathematics, not the other way around.

16
00:04:25,279 --> 00:04:52,760
当你学——当你学多元微积分时，会发现全微分就是一个线性映射：从 R^n 到 R^m 的函数在点 x 处的导数是一个线性映射，事实上它就是从 R^n 到 R^m 最好地逼近该函数在该点性态的线性映射。
When you do—when you do calculus of several variables, you'll find that the total derivative is a linear map: of a function from R^n to R^m at a point x is a linear map, and in fact it's the linear map from R^n to R^m that best approximates the function at that point.

17
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:57,871
这就是线性算子从微积分引入数学的渊源。
So that's where linear operators came into mathematics, out of calculus.

18
00:04:57,871 --> 00:05:10,813
如果你以为在任意域上情况都一样——可别想得太简单。举例来说，如果 F 是实数域，你考虑这个从 V 到 W 的求导映射，对吧？
Now if you think there are things that change over an arbitrary field—you shouldn't think it's that easy. So for example, if you do this where F is the real numbers, and you consider this differentiation map from V to W, right?

19
00:05:10,813 --> 00:05:16,282
V 的维数是 n + 1，W 的维数是 n。那么你可以问：该映射是满射吗？
The dimension of V is n + 1, the dimension of W is n. So you can ask, is the map surjective?

20
00:05:16,282 --> 00:05:29,270
它有核吗，等等？次数不超过 n - 1 的每个多项式都是某个不超过 n 次的多项式的导数吗？是的，这并不难，那么映射的核是什么？
Does it have a kernel, etc.? So is every polynomial of degree n - 1 or less a derivative of a polynomial of degree n? Yeah, that's not so hard, and what's the kernel of the mapping?

21
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:40,334
导数为零的函数是常数，所以它有一个一维的核，并且是满射。
Well, the kernel of the functions who have derivative zero are the constants, so this would have a one-dimensional kernel and it would be surjective.

22
00:05:40,334 --> 00:05:56,380
但在任意域上这就不成立了！大家可以思考一下：当比如F = Z/pZ 时，d/dx 的核是什么？
That's not true over an arbitrary field! So you might try to think about: what is the kernel—is the kernel of d/dx when, say, for example, F is equal to Z/pZ?

23
00:05:56,380 --> 00:06:14,855
这是一个完全合法的域。当然它总是包含常数：T 的核总是包含 F。每当你对常数求导时都会得到 0。
That's a perfectly good field. Well, it always contains the constants: kernel of T contains F always. Whenever you differentiate a constant you get 0.

24
00:06:14,855 --> 00:06:28,090
但——但如果 n >= p，即多项式的次数大于等于 p，T 是否也把多项式 x^p 包含在核中？
But—but if n is bigger than or equal to p, the degree of the polynomial is bigger than equal to p, does T also have polynomial x^p in the kernel?

25
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:43,788
因为按通常公式，x^p 对 x 的导数是 p x 的p - 1 次方，看起来很正常，但在 Z/pZ 中乘以 p 就是乘以 0，别忘了！
Because the derivative with respect to x of x^p is, by our usual formula, p x to the p - 1, which looks pretty good, except multiplication by p is 0 in Z/pZ, remember!

26
00:06:43,788 --> 00:07:00,969
所以当你在一般域上工作时，各种奇奇怪怪的事情都会发生！但它依然是一个线性算子。好的，这是一个很有趣的问题：一般情况下的核和余核是什么？大家可以思考一下。
So all kinds of strange things can start happening when you work on general fields, but still it's a linear operator. Okay, so that's an interesting question: what's the kernel and cokernel in the general case? You might think about that.

27
00:07:00,969 --> 00:07:14,739
好的，现在如果我们有一个线性算子，我们像之前定义群同态那样定义 T 的核：它是使得 T(v) = 0 的向量 v ∈ V 的集合，它是 V 的一个子空间。
All right, now if we have a linear operator, we define the kernel of T as before, like for a group homomorphism: is a set of vectors v in V such that T(v) is equal to zero, and that's a subspace in V.

28
00:07:14,739 --> 00:07:40,709
我们定义 T 的像为所有形如T(v) 的向量 w ∈ W 的集合，它是 W 的子空间。我们将证明一个关于这些空间维数的宏大公式，这就是我们的——这是我们的维数公式，
And we define the image of T as the set of vectors w in W which are of the form T of V, and that's a subspace of W. And we're going to prove a big formula about the dimensions of these spaces. So here's our—here's our dimension formula, which we've already proved in various guises,

29
00:07:40,709 --> 00:08:07,278
虽然我们之前以不同形式证明过，但这个结论怎么强调都不为过：V 的维数等于核的维数加上 T 的像的维数。特别地，看刚才的例子：该映射为满射当且仅当它的核维数为 1。
but can't do it—you can't do this one too many times: that the dimension of V is the dimension of the kernel plus the dimension of the image of T. So in particular, you take this case: this map is surjective if and only if its kernel has dimension 1.

30
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:31,291
因此在刚才那个域上核中出现更多元素这一事实，就表明该映射不可能是满射，因为核至少是二维的。有人能看出 W 中哪个多项式不在像中吗？因为 x^p在核中？
So the fact that in the case where we were over this field we had more elements in the kernel would indicate that the map couldn't be surjective in that case, because we had at least a two-dimensional kernel. Can someone see some polynomial in W which is not in the image, because x^p is in the kernel?

31
00:08:31,291 --> 00:08:43,489
非常好！W 中的 x^{p-1} 就不在像中，因为如果你愿意，这就像——有点类似于1/x 在通常微积分求导中不在像中一样，你必须引入新函数；
Very good! x^{p-1} in W is not in the image, because if you want, it's just like—kind of just like 1/x is not in the image of differentiation in the general case,

32
00:08:43,489 --> 00:08:53,718
这里没有任何函数、没有任何 x^p 的倍数的导数会非零，因为有这个公式，所以你永远打不到这个——这个多项式。很酷吧。好的，我们来证明这个定理。
you have to have a new function, and there's—there's no function, no multiple of x to the p will ever have nonzero derivative because of this formula, so you'll never hit this—this polynomial.

33
00:08:53,718 --> 00:09:32,613
证明：设 {v_1, ..., v_k} 为 ker T 的一组基，并将其扩充为V 的一组基 {v_1, ..., v_k, v_{k+1}, ..., v_n}。
Cool. All right, so let's prove this. Proof: let v_1 through v_k be a basis of the kernel of T, and extend this to a basis v_1 through v_k and then v_{k+1} up to v_n of V.

34
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:43,021
换句话说，我们先取这些——首先你总是可以这么做，它是子空间所以有基，有限维向量空间必有基；
So in other words, we take these first—you can always, first of all, this a subspace so it has a basis, finite dimensional vector spaces have bases;

35
00:09:43,021 --> 00:10:12,223
一旦我们有了一个线性无关子集（它在 V 中显然线性无关），就可以通过不断添加向量直到得到生成集来扩充为整个向量空间的基，且保持线性无关。
and once we have a subset which is linearly independent, which we know it is in V, since linearly independent in V we can extend to a basis of the vector space by continuing to add one vector until we get to a spanning set, all still linearly independent.

36
00:10:12,850 --> 00:10:37,896
好的。证明本定理的核心断言：向量 w_i = T(v_{k+i}) 是 T 的像的一组基，换言之，w_1 = T(v_{k+1})，一直到 w_{n-k} = T(v_n)。
Okay. Claim that will prove our theorem: then w_i is equal to T of v_{k+i} is a basis for the image of T.

37
00:10:37,896 --> 00:11:06,875
所以如果你取这些剩余基向量的像，记为 w_1, w_2 等等，那么它就是像的一组基。
In other words, w_1 is T of v_{k+1} all the way down to w_{n-k} which is T of v_n. So if you take the image of these remaining basis vectors over here and you call this w_1 and this w_2, etc., then that's a basis of the image.

38
00:11:06,875 --> 00:11:21,752
如果这是真的我们就证完了，因为此时核的维数是 k，像的维数是 n - k，这两者相加正好等于 V 的维数 n。所以如果我们能证明这个断言，就得到了所谓的计数定理。
And if that's true we're done, because the dimension and the kernel here would be k, and the dimension of the image would be n - k, and those two things would add up to the dimension of V which is n. So if we can prove this statement, we have this what they call the counting formula.

39
00:11:21,752 --> 00:11:29,164
好的，首先要证明它们是一组基，必须验证它们能张成且线性无关。
Okay, well, the first is to prove that they are a basis, you have to check that they span and that they're linearly independent.

40
00:11:29,164 --> 00:11:56,151
张成性很容易：因为像中的任意 w都是 T(v)，可以写成 T(∑_{i=1}^k a_i v_i + ∑_{i=k+1}^nb_i v_i)。
So spanning is easy, because they span as any w in the image is T of V, can be written as T of the summation from i equal 1 to k of a_i times v_i plus the summation from k plus 1 up to n of b_i v_i.

41
00:11:56,151 --> 00:12:03,160
因为这些 v_i 构成了 V 的基，所以 V 中的任意向量都可以写成各项之和。
So any vector in V, because these v_i gave a basis of V, can be written as a sum of terms.

42
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:07,980
这些项在线性变换下全部映为 0，因为这些 v_i 属于核。
These terms under the transformation all go to 0 because the v_i are in the kernel.

43
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:24,056
由于 T 是同态，这等于 ∑_{i=1}^k a_i T(v_i)加上 ∑_{i=k+1}^n b_i T(v_i)——这是因为 T 是同态。
This, because it's a homomorphism, is the summation of a_i T of v_i, i equal 1 to k, plus the summation from k plus 1 to n of b_i T of v_i—that's because T is a homomorphism.

44
00:12:24,056 --> 00:12:29,844
前面这些全都是 0，因为原始向量被选作核的基。
These are all 0 because the original vectors were chosen to be basis of the kernel.

45
00:12:29,844 --> 00:12:52,175
所以这就只剩下 ∑ b_i T(v_i)，也就是∑_{i=1}^{n-k} b_i w_i。这就表明值域中的任意向量都是这些w_i 的线性组合，因此它们张成像空间。
So this is the summation of b_i T of v_i, which is the same as the summation of b_i w_i from i equal 1 to n minus k. And that shows that any vector in the range is a linear combination of the w's, so they span.

46
00:12:52,175 --> 00:12:58,130
第二点：它们线性无关。
Second thing: they are linearly independent.

47
00:13:01,090 --> 00:13:16,920
假设我们——假设我们有一个线性关系，写成 ∑_{i=1}^{n-k} b_i w_i = 0。
So we assume that—assume we have a relation, and our relation we write is the summation of b_i w_i is equal to zero.

48
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:27,143
我们必须证明所有 b_i 全为 0。
So we have to show that um that those things are that the b_i are all zero.

49
00:13:27,143 --> 00:13:56,110
考虑向量求和 ∑ b_i v_{k+i}，即 i 从 1 到 n - k 的 ∑ b_i v_{i+k}——换句话说，将这个关系拉回到 V：即每个 v_{i+k} 都映为 w_i。
So consider the vector summation of b_i v_{k+i}, where i goes from k plus 1—well, let's go from i equal 1 to n minus k, and b_i times v_{i+k}. In other words, pull this relation back to V: namely, these v_{i+k} map to the w_i.

50
00:13:56,110 --> 00:14:17,800
考虑 V 中的这个向量，我们不妨称它为 v_0。我断言 T(v_0) = 0。为什么？
So consider this vector in V, let's call this vector v_0 or something. I claim that T of v_0 is equal to 0. Why?

51
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:40,202
因为 T 作用于该向量就等于这个和式，而该和式已被假设为 W 中的零向量。这对 v_0 意味着什么？如果 T(v_0) = 0，这意味着v_0 怎样？
Because T of this vector is this vector, and this vector was assumed to be the zero vector in W. What does that mean about v_0? If T of v_0 is 0, what does that say about v_0?

52
00:14:40,202 --> 00:14:42,913
它属于核！
It's in the kernel!

53
00:14:42,913 --> 00:14:58,907
好的，既然 v_0 属于核，我们就可以用我们核的一组基来表示它：∑_{i=1}^k a_i v_i。
Okay, since v_0 is in the kernel, we can express it in terms of the basis of our kernel: i equal 1 to k a_i v_i.

54
00:14:58,907 --> 00:15:22,848
但另一方面，按定义它也是 ∑_{i=1}^{n-k} b_i v_{i+k}，因为这是 v_0 的定义；前者是因为它属于核，且 V 的这组基中的前几个元素构成了核的基，
But on the other hand, it's also the summation from i equal 1 to n minus k b_i v_{i+k}, because this was the definition of v_0, and this follows because it's in the kernel, and these elements, the first elements in our basis of V,

55
00:15:22,848 --> 00:15:46,776
所以可以这样表示。这给了我们一个线性关系：于是 ∑_{i=1}^k a_i v_i 减去∑_{i=1}^{n-k} b_i v_{i+k} 等于 0。这是关于 v_i 的一个线性关系！
give a basis of the kernel, so we can express it, and that gives us a linear relation: hence the summation of a_i v_i from 1 to k minus the summation of b_i v_{i+k} from 1 to n minus k is equal to 0. That's a linear relation on the v_i!

56
00:15:46,776 --> 00:16:12,867
这些 v_i 是被扩充成为基的，因此它们线性无关。这是我们 V 的基上的线性关系，所以所有 a_i = 0 且所有 b_i = 0。
The v_i where this thing was extended to be a basis, so they were linearly independent. This is a linear relation on our basis of V, so all a_i equals 0 and all b_i equals 0.

57
00:16:12,867 --> 00:16:25,224
既然所有 b_i 都等于 0，我们就证明了向量 w_i 是线性无关的，因为只要有一个线性关系，我们就证明了 b_i全为 0。
And since all the b_i are equal to zero, we've just shown that the vectors w_i are linearly independent, because any time we had a relation we've just proved the b_i zero.

58
00:16:25,224 --> 00:16:36,459
证毕！这并不难，而且我们以不同形式做过好几次类似的论证，但理解它很有好处。
Done! This isn't difficult, and we've done this kind of argument a few times in different guises, but it's nice to understand.

59
00:16:36,459 --> 00:16:44,668
所以这是一个基础的计数定理，在向量空间理论中无处不在：如果你在两个同维数的向量空间之间有一个映射，
So this is a fundamental counting formula which is used all the time in vector space theory: if you have a map between two vector spaces of the same

60
00:16:44,668 --> 00:17:05,980
你想证明它是满射，只需证明它的核为零。对吧？好的，它的另一个推论——我能擦掉一部分黑板吗？当然，为什么不呢。
dimension and you want to prove its surjective, all you have to do is prove it has no kernel. Okay? Okay, another corollary of this—can I erase some of this? Sure, why not.

61
00:17:11,859 --> 00:17:41,279
叙述这个推论的另一种方式：若 V 是有限维的，W 是 V 的子空间，则 W 的维数加上商空间 V/W 的维数等于 V 的维数：dim W + dim(V/W) = dim V。
Another way of stating this corollary: if V is finite-dimensional and W is a subspace of V, then dimension of W plus the dimension of the quotient space V over W is equal to the dimension of V.

62
00:17:41,279 --> 00:18:19,655
证明：存在一个从 V 到商空间的同态 T，将向量映为它关于 W 的陪集，该映射是满射且核为 W。对吧？只要有子空间，就会诱导一个到商空间的同态。
Proof: there is a homomorphism T from V to the quotient space taking a vector to its coset of W, which is surjective with kernel W. Right? We have—any time we have a subspace it gives us a homomorphism to the quotient space.

63
00:18:19,655 --> 00:18:32,499
这是满射，所以像的维数就是这里的商空间维数，核的维数就是 W 的维数，由此得证。
This is onto, so the dimension of the image is this dimension here, the dimension of the kernel is the dimension of W, hence this.

64
00:18:32,499 --> 00:19:01,990
好，顺便说一句，这些概念在文献中都有专门名称，因为核与像这些基本概念在数学的不同领域早在被形式化之前就已广泛出现：像的维数有时被称为 T 的秩（rank），核的维数有时被称为 T 的零度（nullity）。
Okay, now by the way these things have names in the literature, because these fundamental concepts of kernel and image arose in a lot of different places in mathematics before they were all formalized: so the image—the dimension of the image is sometimes called the rank of T, this is sometimes called the nullity of T.

65
00:19:01,990 --> 00:19:09,208
线性代数的发展史非常有趣。正如我所说，它脱胎于微积分；许多精妙的思想都源自微积分。
Development of linear algebra is a very interesting subject. As I say, it grew out of calculus; a lot of subtle things came out of calculus.

66
00:19:09,208 --> 00:19:16,390
我们最终会讲到正交群和二次型——那也是微积分中二阶导数检验的产物。
We're going to eventually get to orthogonal groups and quadratic forms—that also came out of calculus when you did the second derivative test.

67
00:19:16,390 --> 00:19:33,884
如果你们中有人学过多变量微积分，就会知道一阶导数是线性算子，而从 R^n 到 R 的函数的二阶导数是一个 n × n 对称矩阵（Hessian 矩阵），它给出了一个二次型，其正负特征值的个数揭示了关于鞍点的各种信息。
If any of you have studied multivariable calculus, you know that the first derivative is a linear operator, the second derivative of a function from R^n to R is an n by n symmetric matrix which gives a quadratic form, and the number of positive and negative eigenvalues tells you all kinds of things about saddle points.

68
00:19:33,884 --> 00:19:53,364
这一切都脱胎于微积分；而我们今天所学的线性代数直到 19 世纪末才被完全公理化。好的。上次 Peter 讲了一点矩阵的内容，我来复习一下。
That all grew out of calculus; and linear algebra as we study it today was only formalized at the end of the 19th century. Okay. Now Peter talked a little bit about matrices last time and I'm going to review that.

69
00:19:53,364 --> 00:19:58,912
大家不必在这上面走火入魔：在 19 世纪末期，人们对矩阵彻底痴迷。
One shouldn't get too carried away with this: the end of the 19th century people became totally carried away with matrices.

70
00:19:58,912 --> 00:20:12,010
如果你去卡博特图书馆的地下室，会看到一排又一排 19 世纪的矩阵代数书籍，人们忽视了他们所讨论的本质上全都是线性算子——他们完全陷入到了记号之中！
If you go to the basement of Cabot library, you can find shelves and shelves of 19th century books which are about matrix algebra, and people lost sight of the fact that all they were talking about was linear operators—they got so involved with the notation!

71
00:20:12,010 --> 00:20:28,633
因此让我们回顾矩阵是如何产生的：当你有一个向量空间 V 并选定它的一组基 {v_1, ..., v_n}；然后我们有另一个向量空间 W，并选定它的一组基 {w_1, ..., w_m}。
So let's recall how matrices come up. When you have a vector space V and you pick a basis for it, v_1 through v_n; then we're going to have another vector space W, and we're going to pick a basis for it, w_1 through w_m.

72
00:20:28,633 --> 00:20:58,139
正如 Peter 上次向大家展示的那样，一组基给出了 V 与有限维向量空间 F^n 之间的同构，它将任意向量 v 映为其在该基下的坐标：你把 v 写成 ∑_{i=1}^n a_i v_i。
Now the basis, as I think Peter showed you last time, a basis gives an isomorphism between V and the finite dimensional vector space F^n, which takes an arbitrary vector v to its coordinates with respect to this basis.

73
00:20:58,139 --> 00:21:09,357
这是唯一的表达式，因为这是一组基，你将 v 映为 n 元组 (a_1, a_2, ..., a_n)。
So you write v is the summation of a_i v_i, i equal 1 to n. Now that's a unique expression, because this is a basis, and you map v to the n-tuple (a_1, a_2, ..., a_n).

74
00:21:09,357 --> 00:21:21,720
两个向量相加，坐标也相应相加；标量乘以向量，坐标也乘以该标量。所以这里有一个自然同态，事实上它是一个同构。
And if you add vectors, you add their coordinates, and if you multiply a vector by a scalar, you multiply its coordinate. So you've got a natural homomorphism here, which is in fact an isomorphism.

75
00:21:23,750 --> 00:21:35,100
它显然是满射，因为任意坐标都对应一个向量；它的核为零，因为如果一个向量的坐标全为零，那么该向量就是零向量。
It's clearly onto because any coordinate gives you a vector, and its kernel is zero because if the coordinates of a vector are all zero, then the vector is the zero vector.

76
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:44,284
因此选定一组基，就在你的抽象空间与这个非常具体的空间之间建立了一个向量空间同构。
So a choice of a basis gives you an isomorphism of vector spaces between your abstract space and this very concrete space.

77
00:21:44,284 --> 00:21:52,580
同样地，W 的基给出了 W 到 F^m 的同构，一个类似的同构。
Likewise, your basis of W gives you an isomorphism from W to F^m, similar isomorphism.

78
00:21:52,580 --> 00:22:24,206
现在的问题是：一旦选定了这些同构，线性算子看起来是怎样的？一旦选定了这些同构——这就是引出矩阵的核心问题。
Now the question is: what does a linear operator look like once we've chosen these isomorphisms? Once these isomorphisms have been chosen, that's the big question that leads to matrices.

79
00:22:24,206 --> 00:22:29,852
所以显然，如果你有一个从 V 到 W 的线性映射并在两端选取同构，它将诱导出一个从 F^n 到 F^m 的线性映射。
So obviously, it's going—if you have a linear map from V to W and you choose an isomorphism here, it's going to give you a linear map from F^n to F^m.

80
00:22:29,852 --> 00:22:54,366
因此我们会得到一个像这样的小图表，允许我写下来：这是线性算子 T，这是同构（我用箭头下的波浪线表示）到 F^n，这是到 F^m 的同构。问题是：一旦我们利用该同构，从 F^n 到 F^m 的映射看起来是怎样的？
So we're going to have little diagram that looks like this, if you'll let me write it: here's our linear operator T, here's our isomorphism which I'll denote by a little squiggle under the arrow with F^n, here's our isomorphism here with F^m, and the question is: what does it look like over on this map from F^n to F^m once we use this isomorphism?

81
00:22:54,366 --> 00:23:26,613
好，我们稍后回到这里。我们先来看看基在线性算子作用下的表现。如果我把线性算子作用在 V 的基上，每一个 T(v_i)——对 V 的基中的每个向量，只要作用线性算子就会得到 W 中的一个向量，我可以将其按W 的基展开。
Okay, we'll come back to that. Well, let's see what this basis does with a linear operator. If I apply the linear operator to a basis of V, each T of v_i—for every vector in the basis of V, if I apply my linear operator I get a vector in W, and I can write it out in terms of my basis of W.

82
00:23:26,613 --> 00:23:51,297
事实上我对 v_j 这么写：T(v_j) 等于 ∑_{i=1}^m a_{ij}乘以 w_i，其中 j = 1, 2, 直到 n。这些 a_{ij} 都是域 F 中的元素，对吧？
So in fact I'll do it for v_j: is the summation, sorry, over i equal 1 to m of a_{ij} times w_i, and that is for j equal 1, 2, all the way up to n. And these a_{ij} are elements in my field F, right?

83
00:23:51,297 --> 00:24:01,662
因为当我把 T 作用在 V 的基向量上时得到 W 中的向量，我可以把它唯一写成 w_i 的线性组合。
Because when I apply T to my basis vector of V, I get a vector in W, and I can write it as a linear combination of the w_i uniquely.

84
00:24:01,662 --> 00:24:19,762
所以这些 a_{ij} 是由 T 以及基的选取所唯一确定的 F 中的元素。你必须选定两组基才能得到 a_{ij}，否则不行。
So these a_{ij} are elements in F determined by T and the choice of basis. And you have to choose both bases before you get the a_{ij}, otherwise couldn't do it.

85
00:24:19,762 --> 00:24:28,952
反过来，如果我有了 V 和 W 的基，并且给你这些 a_{ij}，它们就唯一确定了T！
Conversely, if I have bases of V and W and I give you these a_{ij}, they determine T!

86
00:24:28,952 --> 00:24:38,676
这些标量 a_{ij} 决定了 T。
The scalars a_{ij} determine T.

87
00:24:38,676 --> 00:25:08,979
你需要它们全部：i 从 1 到 n，j 从 1 到 m——抱歉，j 等于——抱歉，我们讲得有点急了：j 从 1 到 n，i 从 1 到 m。所以共有 mn 个标量，mn 个标量决定了线性变换 T。
You need all of them: i equal 1 to n, j equal 1 to m—sorry, j is equal—sorry, we're going— getting a little ahead of ourselves here: j is equal to 1 up to n, i is equal to 1 up to m. So mn scalars, mn scalars determine the transformation T.

88
00:25:08,979 --> 00:25:21,227
为什么？因为如果我想知道 T 对 V 中任意向量的作用，只需将 v 写成v_j 的线性组合；我知道 T(v_j) 是什么，因而就知道 T 对任何向量的作用！
Why? Because if I want to know what T does to any vector of V, I write v as a linear combination of the v_j; I know what T of v_j is, so therefore I know what T of anything is!

89
00:25:21,227 --> 00:25:39,558
即写出 v 等于∑_{j=1}^n x_j v_j；那么 T(v) 等于 ∑_{j=1}^n x_j T(v_j)，
Why, write v is equal to the summation of x_j v_j, j equal 1 to n; then T of v is equal to the summation from j equal 1

90
00:25:39,558 --> 00:26:00,520
也就是∑_{i=1}^m (∑_{j=1}^n a_{ij} x_j) w_i，这告诉我结果向量是什么。所以我知道 T 对任意向量的作用——这就是公式！
to n x_j times T of v_j, which is the summation a_{ij} from i equal one to m of w_i, and that tells me what the vector is. So I know what T does to any vector, it's a formula!

91
00:26:00,520 --> 00:26:09,101
好，现在如果把这个公式写得更精确，它就是一个矩阵乘法——这才是核心所在！
Okay, now if you make that formula precise, it's a matrix multiplication—that's the big thing here!

92
00:26:09,101 --> 00:26:38,952
为了精确表述，如果我们定义 A 为m × n 矩阵 (a_{ij})——这意味着（我总是这样记）：把 T(v_j) 的像放在第 j 列，这些就是向量 T(v_j) 关于基 {w_i} 的坐标。
So that to make this precise, if we define A to be the m by n matrix a_{ij}, which means—and I always remember it this way—that you put the image of T of v_j in the j-th column, and these are the coordinates of the vector T of v_j with respect to the basis w_i.

93
00:26:38,952 --> 00:27:07,480
好的，那么如果我们把这个公式写出来，写成 y 的求和——让我们把它改写为 ∑_{i=1}^m y_i w_i：那么我们会发现 y_i 是通过用该矩阵作用在 x_j 上得到的。
Okay, then this formula is given, if we wrote this out as a formula as a summation of y—let's rewrite it here as the summation of y_i w_i, i equal 1 to m: then we would find that the y's are given by taking this matrix and applying it to the x_j's.

94
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:35,361
所以 Y 作为一个——列向量，即 (y_1, ..., y_m)^T，等于 A X，也就是 A 乘以列向量 (x_1, ..., x_n)^T。这就是公式所表达的。
So Y as a—as a column vector, which means y_1 down to y_m, is equal to A X, which means A applied to the column vector x_1 down to x_n. That's what that formula says.

95
00:27:35,361 --> 00:27:57,142
因此对应于一个线性变换以及在两空间中基的选取，我们得到一组标量，mn 个标量，我们将其排成一个矩阵；线性变换就是由该矩阵的作用给出的，即用该矩阵左乘该向量。
So that associated to a linear transformation and the choices of bases on the first base and the second we get a collection of scalars, mn scalars, which we put into a matrix; and that the linear transformation is given by applying that matrix, left multiplying that matrix times the vector.

96
00:27:57,142 --> 00:28:14,300
换句话说，图表就这样被补全了：这里的映射就是用矩阵 A 左乘，其中这被视为一个列向量，而这则是结果列向量。
In other words, this diagram fills in like this: this map here is left multiplication by the matrix A, where this is considered as an a column vector and this is the resulting column vector.

97
00:28:14,300 --> 00:28:22,884
Peter，你在赎罪日讲了这个，对吧？赎罪日总得受点苦，你讲的就是这个吧。
Peter, you did this on Yom Kippur, right? It should be a certain amount of suffering on Yom Kippur, that's what you had, yes.

98
00:28:22,884 --> 00:29:14,495
对，让我们停顿一下——这里的指标很多，把指标理清楚非常重要。是的，我认为这里应该是 i；我对 v 一直用 j，因为它们对应列向量，而对 w 用 i。
Let's pause—there are a lot of indices here, and it's really important to get the indices right. Yes, you know, I think these should be i's; I've been using j's for the v's because those turn out to be like the column vectors, and i's for the w's.

99
00:29:14,495 --> 00:29:21,070
因此如果你写下来，正如我所说，你必须综合这个公式，看看如何由此得出 y_i，而它正是矩阵乘法，这就是核心断言！
So if you write it, so as I say you have to work this formula together and see how you get y_i out of this, and it's a matrix multiplication, that's the claim!

100
00:29:21,070 --> 00:29:49,735
矩阵乘法就是：取我刚才定义的矩阵 A。让我们看一个例子，做个例子无伤大雅。好，大家都明白是怎么回事了吗？例：考虑映射 T: V -> W，其中每个都是二维空间。
And the matrix multiplication is: you take the matrix A that I've defined in this way. Let's do an example, let's do an example, it can't hurt. Okay, so everyone sees how this works? Example: let's take the map T from V to W, where each are two-dimensional.

101
00:29:49,735 --> 00:30:02,918
V 有一组基 {v_1, v_2}，W 有一组基——抱歉，基 {w_1, w_2}。
V has a basis v_1, v_2, and W has a basis w—sorry, basis w_1, w_2.

102
00:30:02,918 --> 00:30:15,464
并且假设 T(v_1) = 2 w_1，且 T(v_2) = 3 w_1 + 4 w_2。好的，这可以作为基表述下的线性算子示例。
And suppose that T of v_1 is 2 w_1, and T of v_2 is 3 w_1 plus 4 w_2. Okay, that could be an example of a linear operator in terms of the basis.

103
00:30:15,464 --> 00:30:42,359
那我得到的矩阵就是以下 2×2 矩阵：在第一列我放入T(v_1) 关于基 {w_1, w_2} 的坐标——你得把它看作 2 w_1 + 0 w_2——所以第一列将是 [2, 0]^T；第二列 T(v_2) 则是 [3, 4]^T。
Then the matrix I would get would be the following 2x2 matrix: in the first column I put the coordinates of T of v_1 in terms of the basis w_1, w_2—so you have to see this as 2 w_1 + 0 w_2—so the first column would be 2 0; the second column, T of v_2, would be 3 4.

104
00:30:42,359 --> 00:31:07,030
现在假设 V 中有一个向量是 7 v_1 + 8 v_2，我想看看线性算子作用在它上面的结果。我可以直接把它代入这个公式，对吧？
Now suppose I had a vector in V which was the vector 7 v_1 plus 8 v_2, and I—and I wanted to see what the linear operator did to it. Now what I could do is just substitute it in with this formula, right?

105
00:31:07,030 --> 00:31:23,855
我可以这样算：T(v_1) = 2 w_1，所以 T(7 v_1) = 14 w_1；T(v_2) 是这个，所以 T(8 v_2)是 24 w_1 + 32 w_2；把它们加在一起重新整理。但我也可以做矩阵乘法！
I could say: well, T of v_1 is 2 w_1, so T of 7 v_1 is 14 w_1; T of v_2 is this, so T of 8 v_2 is 24 of w_1 plus 32 w_2, add them all together and reassemble. But I could also do the matrix multiplication!

106
00:31:23,855 --> 00:31:58,352
我可以指出T(v) 由矩阵 A 乘以列向量 [7, 8]^T 给出，它等于列向量 [14 + 24 = 38，0 + 32 = 32]^T，这意味着 T(v) = 38 w_1 + 32 w_2。
I could say that T of V is given by the matrix A times the column vector 7 8, which is equal to the column vector 14 plus 24, 38, 0 plus 32, which means that T of V is equal to 38 w_1 plus 32 w_2.

107
00:31:58,352 --> 00:32:13,207
所以这只是换种方式重写一个事实：一旦知道了变换在基上的作用，就掌握了整个变换；这些标量告诉我们变换对基的作用，
So this is just a way of rewriting the fact that we know a transformation once we know it on the basis, and these scalars tell us what the transformation does to the basis,

108
00:32:13,207 --> 00:32:30,190
因此必然有一种方法从这些标量中恢复线性变换，而秘诀就是矩阵乘法！这就是为什么矩阵乘法如此重要。好的，这清楚了吗？还有其他问题吗？
so there must be a way of recovering the linear transformation from all these scalars, and the recipe is matrix multiplication! That's why matrix multiplication is important. Okay, did that help? Other questions?

109
00:32:30,190 --> 00:32:33,644
这太重要了，大家必须彻底搞清楚。
This is so important, you got to get it all right.

110
00:32:33,644 --> 00:32:53,420
特别地，我们以后会经常用到：如果 V 等于W，我们只选取一组基，且有一个从 V 到 V 的线性变换，
Now in particular, and we're going to use this a lot: if V is equal to W, and we just choose one basis, and we have a linear transformation from V to V,

111
00:32:53,420 --> 00:33:18,460
那么通常会用同一组基来表示该变换，即定义域和值域使用同一组基。这就是所谓的自同态——即从一个向量空间到自身的同态。
then it's customary to write the transformation in terms of this one basis where you use it both on the domain and on the range. So this is what we would call an endomorphism—that means a homomorphism from a vector space to itself.

112
00:33:18,460 --> 00:33:26,386
这时我们得到一个方阵：T 关于定义域和值域相同基的矩阵。
Then we get a square matrix: matrix of T with respect to the same basis of domain and range.

113
00:33:26,386 --> 00:33:46,465
这是自然合理的，因为定义域和值域是同一个空间，它等于一个 n × n 矩阵。这才是我们真正大显身手的地方！
That makes sense because the domain and range are the same space, is equal to an n by n matrix. That's where we're really going to use this!

114
00:33:46,465 --> 00:34:34,641
这非常酷：如果我们有另一个自同态，如果我们有两个从 V 到 V 的映射 S 和 T，在基 B 下，T 的矩阵为A，S 的矩阵为 B，二者都是 n × n 矩阵，我们想知道复合映射 S ∘ T（也是从 V 到 V 的新变换）的矩阵是什么？
And this is very cool: if we have another endomorphism: so if we have S and T from V to V, and this is given in terms of the basis B by—this has matrix A and this has matrix B, both n by n matrices, and we want to know what is the matrix of S composed with T, which is a new transformation from V to V?

115
00:34:34,641 --> 00:34:46,673
答案是，当你把它全部展开并用坐标计算时，它正是 B × A，其中这是矩阵乘法！
The answer is, when you blow it all out and you calculate with coordinates etc., it is B times A, where this is matrix multiplication!

116
00:34:46,673 --> 00:34:59,379
这才是矩阵乘法的真正定义！矩阵乘法正是在这里找到了本质：线性算子的复合。这就是为什么矩阵乘法具有结合律。
That is the correct definition of matrix multiplication! That's where matrix multiplication found itself: as the composition of linear operators. That's why matrix multiplication is associative.

117
00:34:59,379 --> 00:35:04,448
这就是矩阵乘法满足结合律的奇迹：因为算子的复合满足结合律！
That's the miracle of why matrix multiplication is associative: because composition of operators is associative!

118
00:35:04,448 --> 00:35:32,679
所以同样地，你必须从矩阵定义和算子复合的定义去验证——这是一场可怕的繁复计算，但结果就是如此。特别地，我们有如下命题。
So again, you must check that from the definition of the matrix and the definition of the composition of operators—it's a horrible computation, but this is what comes out. In particular, we have the following result.

119
00:35:32,679 --> 00:35:59,816
命题：对于线性变换 T: V -> V，以下条件等价：(1) T 是同构，或者说自同构——即向量空间 V 到自身的同构；(2) T 的核为 0；(3) T 的像是整个V；
Proposition: following are equivalent for a transformation T from V to V: (1) T is an isomorphism, or we might say an automorphism—that means an isomorphism from V to itself of vector spaces; (2) the kernel of T is 0;

120
00:35:59,816 --> 00:36:53,384
(4) 若 T 关于基 {v_1, ..., v_n} 的矩阵为 A，则 A 作为n × n 矩阵是可逆的；最后，(5) 矩阵 A 的行列式在域 F 中非零：det(A) ≠ 0。
(3) the image of T is all of V; (4) if the matrix A of T with respect to the basis v_1 through v_n is A, then A is invertible as an n by n matrix; and finally, (5) the determinant of the matrix A is not equal to 0 in the field F.

121
00:36:53,384 --> 00:36:58,646
所以这又是我们已经经历过几次的事情。
So again, this is sort of thing we've been through a couple of times.

122
00:36:58,646 --> 00:37:09,934
我简要比划一下证明思路，好让大家理解：如果你有一个同构，那么它的核显然为 0 且像为全空间。所以 (1) 推出 (2) 和 (3)，这很清楚。
I'll—I'll wave my hands at it so you get the idea: if you have an isomorphism, then its kernel is clearly 0 and its image is everything. So (1) implies (2) and (3), that's clear.

123
00:37:09,934 --> 00:37:15,652
如果满足 (2)，核的维数为 0，那么像的维数就等于 V 的维数。
If you have (2), the kernel has dimension 0, so the image has the dimension of V.

124
00:37:15,652 --> 00:37:24,055
所以像必须是整个 V，因为你可以取像的一组基并扩充为 V 的一组基，但它们元素个数相同，因此像就是整个V。
So the image has to be all of V, because you can take a basis for the image and extend it to a basis for V, but they have the same number of elements, so the image is all of V.

125
00:37:24,055 --> 00:37:35,328
所以它们互推，并且通过维数公式彼此等价。
So this implies this, both of them imply this, and they all imply each other by the formula for dimensions.

126
00:37:35,328 --> 00:37:41,620
如果 T 是一个同构，那么我们可以找到一个逆线性算子将它求逆回到恒等映射。
If T is an isomorphism, then we can—we can find a linear operator that inverts it back to the identity.

127
00:37:41,620 --> 00:37:55,948
由于线性算子的复合就是矩阵乘法，该求逆算子的矩阵就满足与 A 相乘得到单位矩阵的性质。这意味着 A 是可逆矩阵。
And since the composition of linear operators is matrix multiplication, the matrix of that inverting operator would have the property that when you multiplied it by A you'd get the identity. That means A is an invertible matrix.

128
00:37:55,948 --> 00:38:05,164
反过来，如果 A 是可逆矩阵，你会发现 T 的核——也就是矩阵 A 的零度——为 0，并且T 的像是全空间。
Conversely, if A is an invertible matrix, you'll find that the kernel of T—which is the nullity of the matrix A—is 0, and the image of T is everything.

129
00:38:05,164 --> 00:38:08,778
这正是我们对可逆矩阵以及在列向量上的矩阵乘法的认知。
That's really what we know about invertible matrices and matrix multiplication on column vectors.

130
00:38:08,778 --> 00:38:20,450
最后我们见过这通过通常的伴随矩阵等价于矩阵可逆。所以所有这些条件都刻画了什么是同构。
And finally we've seen that this is equivalent to the matrix being invertible by the usual matrix of cofactors. So all of these conditions are what tells you what an isomorphism is.

131
00:38:20,450 --> 00:38:46,935
而所有从 V 到 V 的同构映射 T 的集合构成了群，我想 Peter称之为 GL(V)，它同构于由 F 上行列式非零的 n × n 矩阵构成的群 GL_n(F)。我们最初定义过群 GL_n(R)，对吧？
And the set of T from V to V which are isomorphisms, that forms a group which I think Peter called GL(V), and which is isomorphic to the group GL_n(F) of n by n matrices with nonzero determinant in F. We started off by defining the group GL_n(R) the first time, right?

132
00:38:46,935 --> 00:38:56,657
因此这里我们对任意域都得到了一个可逆 n × n 矩阵构成的乘法群。
So here we get a group for any field of invertible n by n matrices over the field under multiplication.

133
00:38:56,657 --> 00:39:03,520
虽然二者是同一个群，但更好的思考方式将其看作 n 维向量空间在该域上的可逆线性变换群。
And though it's the same as the group, a better way to think of it is invertible linear transformations of an n- dimensional vector space over that field.

134
00:39:03,520 --> 00:39:07,537
顺便说一句，其中有些群是有限群！
So some of these groups, by the way, are finite groups!

135
00:39:07,537 --> 00:39:18,400
所以这是一个有趣的问题：什么是——我们不妨拿一个有限群来热身，然后我将提出我们在周五要深入讨论的另一个问题。
So it's an interesting question: what is—let's just try one of these finite groups just to warm up, and then I'm going to get to another question we're going to get into on Friday.

136
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:37,243
例如，如果 F 是二元域，那么群GL_2(F)，即域 F 上的 2 × 2 可逆矩阵群，是什么？
So for example, if F is the field of two elements, what is the group GL_2(F), 2 by 2 invertible matrices over the field F?

137
00:39:37,243 --> 00:39:50,280
如果你考虑用域 F 中的标量填满一个 2 × 2 矩阵，能构成多少个矩阵？由二元域能构成的矩阵总数是多少？
Well, if you thought about filling up a 2 by 2 matrix with scalars from the field F, how many matrices can you make? What's the total number of matrices I can make out of the field of two elements?

138
00:39:50,280 --> 00:40:08,037
多少个？16 个，对吧！你有 16 种选择，因为 a 可取 0 或 1，b 可取 0 或 1，c 可取 0 或 1，d 可取 0 或 1——共有 16 种2 × 2 矩阵。
How many? 16, right! So you have 16 choices, because a can be 0 or 1, b can be 0 1, c can be 0 1, or d can be 0 1—16 choices of 2 by 2 matrices.

139
00:40:08,037 --> 00:40:13,300
它们并非全可逆。
Well, they're not all—they're not all invertible.

140
00:40:13,300 --> 00:40:29,321
事实上其中有 6 个是可逆的，并且你会发现由此得到了一个 6 阶的有限小群，即二元域上 2 × 2 可逆矩阵在乘法下的群。
So in fact, six of them are invertible, and you'll find so you get a little finite group of order 6, 2 by 2 invertible matrices over the field of two elements under multiplication.

141
00:40:29,321 --> 00:40:41,028
你会发现该群——GL_2(F) 实际上同构于三个字母上的对称群 S_3！怎么看出来呢？
You'll find that this group—and that GL_2(F) is actually isomorphic to the symmetric group on three letters, S_3! How can I see that?

142
00:40:41,028 --> 00:40:54,628
想想这究竟是什么东西，在我们真正看清之前——这就是写下具体矩阵、计算行列式并做繁重运算，与跳出细节看清我们到底在做什么之间的区别。
Well, think about what this thing really is before we actually see—this is the difference between writing down matrices and calculating determinants and doing all these computations, and actually stepping back and seeing what the heck we're doing.

143
00:40:54,628 --> 00:41:09,400
我们所做的就是：该群作用在向量空间 F^2 上。好的，当域包含两个元素时，向量空间 F^2 看起来是怎样的？
So what we're doing is: this group operates on the vector space F squared. All right, what does the vector space F squared look like when the field has two elements in it?

144
00:41:09,400 --> 00:41:18,683
它包含向量 (0, 0)，包含向量 (0, 1)，包含向量 (1, 0)，并且包含向量 (1, 1)。
It has the vector (0, 0) in it, it has the vector (0, 1) in it, it has the vector (1, 0) in it, and it has the vector (1, 1) in it.

145
00:41:18,683 --> 00:41:24,945
仅此而已！在二元域上的二维向量空间中只有四个向量。
That's it! There are only four vectors in the two-dimensional vector space over the field of two elements.

146
00:41:24,945 --> 00:41:33,517
所以如果我有该群中的一个元素，它作用在向量空间上，至少在置换这些向量，对吧？
So if I have an element in this group, it's acting on this vector space, it's permuting these vectors around at the very least, correct?

147
00:41:33,517 --> 00:41:44,297
它必须固定零向量 (0, 0)，因为那是向量空间的原点——任何线性变换都将 0 映为 0。所以它对这三个非零向量进行了置换作用！
It has to fix this vector because that's the origin of the vector space—any linear transformation takes zero to zero. So it's doing a little permutation action on these three vectors!

148
00:41:44,297 --> 00:41:56,290
可以证明你能得到对这三个向量的任意置换，而这当然唯一确定了线性变换。这就给出了它与三个字母上的对称群 S_3 的同构。
Show that you can get any permutation you wish of those three vectors, and that of course determines the linear transformation. So that gives you your isomorphism with the symmetric group on three letters.

149
00:41:56,290 --> 00:42:22,000
很酷吧？非常酷。好的。现在我想再讲一点，因为 Peter 上次提到了：要得到线性变换的矩阵必须选定一组基。那么当你更换基时会发生什么？
Cool, huh? Very cool. Okay. Now I want to make one more point because Peter touched on it last time: to get a matrix for a transformation you have to choose a basis. What happens when you change the basis?

150
00:42:22,000 --> 00:43:01,513
这是一场极其可怕的计算：如果 A 是变换 T: V -> V 关于基 {v_1, ..., v_n} 的矩阵，那么关于另一组基 {v_1', ..., v_n'} 的矩阵是什么？你会得到一个新矩阵 A'。A 与 A'是如何关联的？
So this is truly horrible computation: if A is the matrix of a transformation T from V to V with respect to the basis v_1 through v_n, what is the matrix with respect to a different basis v_1 prime to v_n prime? You got a new matrix A prime. How are A and A prime related?

151
00:43:01,513 --> 00:43:30,900
答案是——关于推导过程我建议大家去看 Artin 的书，因为我从没觉得黑板上的这项推导有启发性——答案是 A' = P A P⁻¹，其中 P 是给出基变换的可逆 n × n 矩阵。
Well, the answer is—and I'm going to let you look at Artin for the computation here, because I've never found this computation to be at all illuminating at the blackboard—that A prime is equal to P A P inverse, where P is the invertible n by n matrix giving the change of basis.

152
00:43:33,099 --> 00:43:47,355
即如果你用一组基表示另一组基的坐标，就给出了矩阵 P。我就不具体讲是谁用谁表示了，太折磨人了！
Namely, if you write the coordinates of one basis in terms of the other basis, that gives you the matrix P. I won't say which basis in terms of which other basis, too horrible!

153
00:43:48,583 --> 00:43:55,126
这个矩阵被称为共轭矩阵。
And you take this—this is called the conjugate matrix.

154
00:43:55,126 --> 00:44:11,704
更一般地，Artin 推导了如下公式：如果你有一个从 V 到 W 的变换，你用矩阵 P 更换 V 的基，用矩阵 Q 更换 W 的基，那么新矩阵就是 Q AP⁻¹。
So more generally, Artin works out the formula: if you have a transformation from V to W, you change your basis on V with the matrix P, you change your basis on W with the matrix Q, then the new matrix is Q A P inverse.

155
00:44:11,704 --> 00:44:17,510
好的。Peter，你做了这个推导吗？你尝试过算它吗？没有，谢天谢地。
Okay. Peter, did you do that? Did you attempt that computation? No, thank God.

156
00:44:17,510 --> 00:44:25,865
好的，仔细看看 Artin 书里的推导，它很重要、很关键。A' 必然有关于 A 的表达式，对吧？
Okay, look carefully at that computation in Artin, it's important, it's critical. There has to be a formula for A prime in terms of A, right?

157
00:44:25,865 --> 00:44:30,315
当你真正推导出来时，就得到了这个优美的共轭公式。
So when you actually work it out, you get this beautiful conjugation formula.

158
00:44:30,315 --> 00:44:46,342
换句话说，如果我们只关心在共轭等价意义下研究这些群中的元素（这对我们极为有用），我们就可以精心选取基，从而可能得到一个形式特别漂亮的矩阵。
In other words, if we're only interested in studying elements in one of these groups up to conjugacy, which is going to be very useful to us, we can choose our basis carefully and get a particularly nice matrix, maybe.

159
00:44:46,342 --> 00:45:12,146
因此这种抽象向量空间的观点——这具有巨大的优势——在于你可以通过选取一个聪明的 V 的基，让线性算子变得更加透明清晰。
So the advantage of this abstract vector space point of view—and it is a tremendous advantage—is that you can render a linear operator more transparent by the choice of an intelligent basis of V.

160
00:45:12,146 --> 00:45:52,868
比起 F^n 观点，以抽象空间 V 为出发点的核心在于：通过选取合适的基，我们可以让算子呈现更简单的形式。
The V point of view over the F to the N point of view is: by choosing a convenient basis we can get a simpler form for our operator.

161
00:45:52,974 --> 00:45:58,680
如果你死盯着一个具体矩阵，你就会被那个矩阵束缚住！我是说，你可能面对一个可怕的矩阵，完全不知道这个算子在做什么。
If you're just fixed on a matrix, you're stuck with that matrix! I mean you might have some horrible matrix and you don't know what the operator is doing at all.

162
00:45:58,680 --> 00:46:18,617
但既然我们只关心背后的线性变换，我们就可以自由选择不同的基，使其对矩阵进行共轭，并可能将其化为简单得多的形式。我们下次就会这么做，当我们讲到——看，有人来电话了。
But since we're only interested in the underlying linear transformation, we should feel free to choose a different basis that will have the property of conjugating the matrix and possibly turning it into a much simpler form. And we're going to be doing that next time when we talk—look at, someone has a call.

163
00:46:18,617 --> 00:46:26,359
好的，让我给大家举一个例子，然后我们就下课。
Okay, let me give you an example of that and then we'll stop.

164
00:46:29,079 --> 00:47:03,951
来自我们第一个命题的例子，也就是映射 T: V -> W 的情形：存在 V 的一组基和 W 的一组基，使得 T 的矩阵呈现极其简单的形式，
Example from our first proposition, the one where we had the map T from V to W: there exists a basis of V and a basis of W so that the matrix of T is particularly simple matrix which looks like this:

165
00:47:03,951 --> 00:47:19,244
看起来像这样：得到一个 r × r 的单位矩阵，其余位置全为零，其中 r等于 T 的秩，即像的维数。
you get the identity matrix, an r by r matrix, and then the rest of the entries are all zeros, where r is equal to the rank of T, the dimension of the image.

166
00:47:19,244 --> 00:47:42,659
于是你得到一个全是 1 和 0 的矩阵，对角线上有 r 个 1，构成一个 r × r 的单位矩阵分块。这在书上写成：[I_r, 0; 0, 0]。不可能有比这更简单的矩阵了！
So you get a matrix of all ones and zeros, and you have r ones running them down the diagonal, a little block like this of r by r identity matrix. So this would be—this is written in the book like this: [I_r 0; 0 0]. Couldn't have a simpler matrix than that!

167
00:47:42,659 --> 00:47:44,477
好的，我们取什么基呢？
Okay, what basis do we take?

168
00:47:44,477 --> 00:48:03,349
我们取 V 的基，首先是那些向量 v_{k+1}直到 v_n，最后是 v_1 到 v_k，其中后面的向量属于核，而前面的向量映为像的基。
Well, we take our basis of V to start off with those vectors v_k plus 1 up to v_n that I called, and then the final ones are v_1 through v_k, where these things are in the kernel and these things map to the basis of the image.

169
00:48:03,349 --> 00:48:13,099
我们取 W 的基为 T(v_{k+1}) 到 T(v_n)，然后把它扩充为 W 的基，其余基向量我们并不关心。
And we take our basis of W to be T of v_{k+1} up to T of v_n, and then we just complete that to be some basis of W that we don't care about the rest of it.

170
00:48:13,099 --> 00:48:28,582
然后看看在第一个命题中发生了什么：这个向量的像就是对应的基向量，所以矩阵的第一列只有一个 1 和全零；下一个向量的像就是下一个基向量，所以第二列在第二个位置为 1，其余全为零。
And then look at—look at what happens in the first proposition: the image of this vector is this vector, so the first column of the matrix just has a 1 and all zeros; the image of the next vector is the next vector, so the second column has a 1 in the second place and all the rest zeros.

171
00:48:28,582 --> 00:48:39,413
一直往下都是如此，而核中那些向量的像全为 0，因为它们属于核。这难道不是一个极其巧妙的基的选取吗？
Same thing happens all the way down here, and the image of these vectors is just 0 because they're in the kernel. So wasn't that a clever choice of basis?

172
00:48:39,413 --> 00:48:56,920
是的。抱歉，是 v_n，非常感谢！所以这些向量的个数是 r，这类向量的个数是 r。抱歉，这里是 v_n，非常感谢。刚才讲得太急了！
Yeah. I'm sorry, v_n, thank you very much! So the number of these vectors is r, the number of such vectors is r. Sorry, this is v_n, thank you very much. Getting a little ahead of myself!

173
00:48:56,920 --> 00:49:03,624
这太容易了，这太容易了，基的选取，因为我们可以分别独立选取 V 和 W 的基。
Now this was too easy, this was too easy, the basis choice, because we had a choice of basis of V and W.

174
00:49:03,624 --> 00:49:27,875
而一个有趣得多的问题是：当我们有一个映射 T: V -> V，且我们只被允许选取一组基，不能独立选取定义域和值域上的基时：我们能否在 V 中选取一组优良的基，使该算子呈现出特别简单的形式？
A much more interesting question is when we have a map T from V to V, and we're only allowed to choose one basis, we're not allowed to choose the basis on the domain and image independently: can we choose a nice basis of V to render this operator particularly simple?

175
00:49:27,875 --> 00:49:36,177
最简单的情况就是如果我们能找到一组所谓的特征向量基——这就引出了特征向量的完整理论！
Well, the simplest way this would happen is if we could find a basis of what are called eigenvectors—this brings in the whole subject of eigenvectors!

176
00:49:36,177 --> 00:49:41,663
特征向量就是使得 T(v) 等于某个标量乘以 v 的向量，它只是被缩放了。
An eigenvector would be a vector such that T of v is some scalar times v, it's just scaled.

177
00:49:41,663 --> 00:49:49,116
如果你有一组由特征向量构成的基，那么矩阵就会是一个对角矩阵，对角线上不全为 1，对吧？
If you had a basis of such, the matrix would be a diagonal matrix, not all ones in it, right?

178
00:49:49,116 --> 00:50:09,589
但如果我们找到这样一组基，那么矩阵就会像这样：diag(c_1, c_2, ..., c_n)，这是一个极易处理的矩阵！
But if we found a basis—if we found a basis of such, then the matrix would look like this: c_1, c_2, c_n, 0, that's an easy matrix to manipulate!

179
00:50:09,589 --> 00:50:20,588
所以这正是我们下次要探讨的：我们总能找到特征向量基吗？何时能，何时不能？如果不能该怎么办？
So that's what we're going to deal with next time: can we always find a basis of eigenvectors? When can we, when can't we? You know, what do we do if we can't?

180
00:50:20,588 --> 00:50:33,675
这就是下一个问题：尝试寻找将特定线性算子化为优良形式的基。这将是周五的主题。好！
That's the next question: to try to find bases that put certain linear operators in nice form. And that'll be the topic for Friday. Good!
